.TH GOFILE-PUBLISH-REMOTE 1 "2026-11-19" "gofile-publish-remote" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gofile-publish-remote \- run gofile-publish on the Proxmox server over ssh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gofile-publish-remote
[\fIOPTIONS\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gofile-publish-remote
is a thin local wrapper that runs
.BR gofile-publish (1)
on the Proxmox server, so recordings are read and uploaded by the machine that
holds them instead of being pulled across the network first. It connects with
.BR ssh (1)
non\-interactively (no TTY, with the host's
.B RemoteCommand
disabled) and executes
.B /usr/local/bin/gofile-publish
with whatever arguments are given.
.P
The token file, state file and manifests therefore live on the server, not on
the desktop.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GOFILE_PUBLISH_SERVER
ssh host to use. Default:
.IR proxmox .
.TP
.B GOFILE_PUBLISH_BIN
Remote executable path. Default:
.IR /usr/local/bin/gofile-publish .
.SH EXAMPLES
Dry run on the server:
.IP
.EX
gofile-publish-remote \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.P
Upload one model:
.IP
.EX
gofile-publish-remote \-\-model abbytheran
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exit status of the remote command, or ssh's own status if the connection fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gofile-publish (1),
.BR ssh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
